  "notes": [
    "Phase A compact smoke stopped after a replayable worker failure; phase B used the corrected engine; phase C broadened content and restarted from committed v1, not random weights.",
    "Phase C survived a workspace reconnection; a later runtime loss required resuming an atomic checkpoint. Counts come from phase counters; raw metrics preserve discarded tails. Plots collapse repeated counters after recovery.",
    "Reward classification uses required companions; custom scripted defeats outside that declaration remain ordinary defeats and retain their raw outcome. Held-out Lantern Road never supplies training rewards.",
    "Only rl- fixtures trained the policy. Existing eight arena maps and Lantern Road authored/flight/fight routes were held out; final tests never selected weights.",
    "Arena held-out cases use four cyclic roster pairings, not all twelve. The four simulation rosters do not cover every new content unit.",
    "Exact resume uses the training engine source plus frozen workload/catalog. The compiler-only tile interning change is after the training source revision; warm start works on changed compatible engine revisions.",
    "Selected policy JSON is formatted for the repository. training_export_sha256 records the original evaluated bytes; gzip recovery retains those bytes."
  ]
